01:24:51,620 --> 01:24:54,340
but people usually are sophisticated enough to realize

130
01:24:54,340 --> 01:24:57,060
that some engineers might dress better than the average engineer.

131
01:24:57,060 --> 01:24:59,500
So, they don't give the really extreme answers.

132
01:24:59,500 --> 01:25:02,380
Rather, they just give an answer that seems to be insensitive to

133
01:25:02,380 --> 01:25:07,060
the actual base rates. And again, that's odd.

134
01:25:07,060 --> 01:25:09,180
And again, like a classic example of using

135
01:25:09,180 --> 01:25:10,900
the representative heuristic or

136
01:25:10,900 --> 01:25:13,500
inappropriately or false positives in medicine,

137
01:25:13,500 --> 01:25:18,620
where because the stereotypical person who is sick will test positive,

138
01:25:18,620 --> 01:25:22,500
people then think people test positive as being sick.

139
01:25:22,500 --> 01:25:25,740
And in fact, if it's very rare to actually be sick,

140
01:25:25,740 --> 01:25:26,980
then this is highly unlikely.

141
01:25:26,980 --> 01:25:28,940
So, think about that horrible airport slogan,

142
01:25:28,940 --> 01:25:30,860
if you see something, say something.

